# Logs, caches, and test captures
**/logs/
**/*.log
**/*.tmp
**/*.bak
# The build writes the real version into wails.json and puts the original back
# when it finishes; this is that original, and it only survives a build the
# machine did not live through.
desktop/wails.json.version-backup
**/.cache/
**/.gradle/
**/coverage/
**/coverage.out
**/*.prof
**/*.trace
/*[Tt]est*.txt
/photo_*.png
/video_*.mp4

# Dependencies and generated output
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.vite/
**/frontend/wailsjs/
**/frontend/package.json.md5
**/bin/
**/build/
!desktop/build/
desktop/build/*
!desktop/build/appicon.icns
!desktop/build/windows/
desktop/build/windows/*
!desktop/build/windows/wails.exe.manifest
**/*.test
**/*.out
**/go.work
**/go.work.sum

# Runtime and release binaries
desktop/clients/*
!desktop/clients/.keep
desktop/cores/*
!desktop/cores/.keep
# The engine is built from source; wintun is a redistributable it loads at
# runtime and cannot build, so it travels with the repo or Windows TUN has
# nothing to create an adapter with on a fresh checkout.
!desktop/cores/wintun.dll
**/*.dmg
**/*.pkg
**/*.msi
**/*.exe
**/*.deb
**/*.rpm
**/*.AppImage
**/*.zip
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.tgz
**/*.7z
**/*.sha256

# Agent working notes, not project source.
memory.md
